cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use hangar in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "hangar: a lightweight module system for small underwater vehicles, with a provenance-recorded learning loop"
abstract: >-
  hangar is a module system for small remotely operated underwater vehicles,
  native to Linux and small enough for the vehicle's own Raspberry Pi. Every
  function of the vehicle is its own process; one manager starts, watches and
  restarts them; they exchange fixed-size messages through shared-memory
  topics, in which every message records, by identifier, the input messages it
  was computed from. That record is what the learning loop builds on: training
  rows joined from provenance, streamed to a trainer on the topside, and weights
  checked by the vehicle before they run.
